write(O/'README.md',b'''# CLOUD-059: preserve the original terminal failure and settle held reads\n\nThis external helper correction retains the original primary scenario error before cleanup, adds a bounded passive wire/UI snapshot, and records cleanup failures separately. The read gate makes at most one terminal operation, records actual request cancellation, settles its known handler before removing interception, fences late unused handlers and preserves diagnostic-write failures. The original absolute8-second gate and application10-second timeout are unchanged. A slow restart can leave its old-read ordering unexercised; no timeout widening, response substitution, admission wait or mutation replay is added.\n\nVersion5 was frozen but not installed. Version6 adds exact Exit payload bytes/SHA256 and only known static representations inside the existing listener chain; unknown payload text remains omitted. It does not alter acceptance expectations or transmitted frames. The original attempt4 hidden error remains unknown. In the separate attempt5 installed capsule, version6 successfully retains FIRST stdout, typed exit0 and the following error/unclean1006 close, which fails the terminal workflow. Useful diagnostics do not constitute a transport correction or full terminal pass.\n\nControlled scopes: original v4 route/scenario10-case run has8 failures/2 controls; final v5 has10 passes, plus3 absolute-budget controls. Earlier6-failure/2-control versus8-pass evidence predates the late-handler review and overlaps. Payload supplement: unchanged test on v5 yields2 expected missing-diagnostic failures/6 controls, v6 yields8 passes; its13 route/budget passes overlap the prior10+3. A first fake-crypto test fixture syntax failure is retained separately. No source counts are added across overlapping runs. Browser WebCrypto itself is exercised only by the separate installed attempt5 receipt, not by the inert Node SHA256 adapter.\n\nOriginal/fixed sources, exact same-test bytes, raw logs, patches and independent source reviews are retained. `historical-complete-manifest.json` documents original full staging directories; this capsule selects relevant members only. Run `python3 verify.py` for publication byte checks. Optional `python3 reproduce.py --node /path/to/node --output /fresh/private/receipt-dir` runs only builtin-node inert fixtures and preserves expected failures; it does not launch an app/browser/Docker/provider. Do not execute archived installed launchers or resume retained fixtures.\n''')
repro='''import argparse,subprocess,json,hashlib,os\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--node',required=True);p.add_argument('--output',required=True);a=p.parse_args();r=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;o=Path(a.output).resolve();o.mkdir(mode=0o700,exist_ok=False)\ncommands=[('route-original','installed-v5/route-settlement.test.mjs',{'C059_ORIGINAL':'1'},1),('route-fixed','installed-v5/route-settlement.test.mjs',{},0),('budget','installed-v5/gate-budget.test.mjs',{},0),('payload-original','installed-v6/scenario.test.mjs',{'C059_PAYLOAD_ORIGINAL':'1'},1),('payload-fixed','installed-v6/scenario.test.mjs',{},0)]\nrows=[]\nfor label,file,extra,want in commands:\n env={k:v for k,v in os.environ.items() if k in ['PATH','LANG','LC_ALL','TZ']};env.update(extra)\n command=[a.node,'--test','--test-concurrency=1',str(r/file)];v=subprocess.run(command,env=env,stdout=subprocess.PIPE,stderr=subprocess.PIPE,timeout=30)\n for stream in ['stdout','stderr']:(o/(label+'.'+stream)).write_bytes(getattr(v,stream))\n row={'label':label,'returncode':v.returncode,'expectedReturncode':want,'command':command};rows.append(row);(o/'result.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows,indent=2)+'\\n');assert v.returncode==want,row\nprint(json.dumps({'inertInvocations':len(rows),'appStarted':False}))\n''';write(O/'reproduce.py',repro.encode())
verify='''from pathlib import Path\nimport hashlib,json\nr=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;m=json.loads((r/'publication.json').read_bytes());count=0\nfor name,v in m['files'].items():\n p=r/name;b=p.read_bytes();assert p.resolve().is_relative_to(r) and len(b)==v['bytes'] and hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()==v['sha256'];count+=1\nprint(json.dumps({'verifiedMembers':count,'runtimeStarted':False}))\n''';write(O/'verify.py',verify.encode());write(O/'assemble.py',Path(__file__).read_bytes())
